@startuml
hide footbox
actor Operator
participant "React UI" as UI
participant "Authenticated HTTP adapter" as Http
participant "analysis application" as Analysis
participant "CustomerActivityPort" as Activity
participant "JpaCustomerActivityAdapter" as ActivityAdapter
participant "PolicyKnowledgePort" as Policy
participant "StaticPolicyAdapter" as StaticPolicy
participant "PgVectorPolicyAdapter" as VectorPolicy
participant "AnalysisModelPort" as Model
participant "DeterministicAnalysisStub" as Deterministic
participant "SpringAiAnalysisAdapter" as LiveAdapter
participant "External AI provider" as Provider
participant "AnalysisHistoryPort" as History
participant "JpaAnalysisHistoryAdapter" as HistoryAdapter
database "PostgreSQL / pgvector" as DB

Operator -> UI : Analyze Customer Activity
UI -> Http : POST analysis request [HTTP/JSON]
Http -> Analysis : analyze(customerId, operatorId) [in-process]
Analysis -> Activity : loadSnapshot(customerId) [in-process]
Activity -> ActivityAdapter : dispatch when R2+ adapter active [in-process]
ActivityAdapter -> DB : JDBC customer/activity/risk queries
DB --> ActivityAdapter : activity + risk evidence
ActivityAdapter --> Activity : CustomerSnapshot projection
Activity --> Analysis : CustomerSnapshot
Analysis -> Policy : retrieveRelevant(context) [in-process]
alt deterministic/offline policy adapter
  Policy -> StaticPolicy : dispatch [in-process]
  StaticPolicy --> Policy : synthetic PolicyEvidence[]
else R4 vector policy adapter
  Policy -> VectorPolicy : dispatch [in-process]
  VectorPolicy -> DB : pgvector query
  DB --> VectorPolicy : retrieved corpus evidence
  VectorPolicy --> Policy : PolicyEvidence[]
end
Policy --> Analysis : PolicyEvidence[] / explicit no-evidence
Analysis -> Model : analyze(context, evidence) [in-process port]
alt deterministic baseline adapter
  Model -> Deterministic : dispatch [in-process]
  Deterministic --> Model : structured candidate / failure
else explicitly configured live adapter
  Model -> LiveAdapter : dispatch [in-process]
  LiveAdapter -> Provider : HTTPS provider API
  Provider --> LiveAdapter : response / network-provider failure
  LiveAdapter --> Model : structured candidate / failure
end
Model --> Analysis : candidate AnalysisResult / failure
Analysis -> Analysis : validate structured result
Analysis -> History : persist(result, customer, operator, time, provenance)
History -> HistoryAdapter : dispatch [in-process]
HistoryAdapter -> DB : JDBC INSERT analysis history
DB --> HistoryAdapter : persisted
HistoryAdapter --> History : analysis identity
History --> Analysis : analysis identity
Analysis --> Http : completed structured analysis
Http --> UI : 200 JSON
UI --> Operator : risk level + findings + recommendations + provenance

note over Policy,Model
  Application-facing ports remain project-owned boundaries. Static/deterministic
  adapters provide the offline path; pgvector/live-provider adapters are R4
  substitutions. JDBC/pgvector and provider HTTPS occur only beyond adapters.
end note
@enduml
